Silence -Wuninitialized in the unit tests.

GCC 16 reports QDQOpKeys values returned by the constexpr GetQDQOpKeys() in
onnxruntime/test/optimizer/qdq_transformer_test.cc as used uninitialized, and
Portage lists them as severe warnings:

  qdq_transformer_test.cc:3528:38: warning: 'qdq_keys.QDQOpKeys::quantize_linear' is used uninitialized [-Wuninitialized]
  qdq_transformer_test.cc:3522:23: note: 'qdq_keys' declared here
   3522 |       const QDQOpKeys qdq_keys = GetQDQOpKeys(false);

The variable is initialized, and the same pattern warns in a small program
outside ONNX Runtime, so this is a compiler false positive. Upstream already
keeps the warning from failing the unit tests, but only when cross compiling,
where HAS_NOERROR is set. The test programs are not installed, so turn the
warning off for them.

--- a/cmake/onnxruntime_unittests.cmake
+++ b/cmake/onnxruntime_unittests.cmake
@@ -184,6 +184,8 @@
     if (${HAS_NOERROR})
       target_compile_options(${_UT_TARGET} PRIVATE "$<$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>:-Wno-error=uninitialized>")
     endif()
+    # GCC reports false positives in the test code.
+    target_compile_options(${_UT_TARGET} PRIVATE "$<$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>:-Wno-uninitialized>")
     onnxruntime_disable_gtest_character_conversion_as_error(${_UT_TARGET})
   endif()
 
